{
  "$comment": "Workspace cutover retirement ledger (#1046; docs/architecture/WORKSPACE-CUTOVER-PLAN.md section 5). One entry per legacy Conductor page, router and backend/stores.py store, with a disposition (PROJECT: rewritten as a Workspace projection on the generated client; RETIRE: deleted; MERGE: folded into another surface; KEEP: outside the Workspace) and a delete-by milestone. The ledger only shrinks: a PR that proves an entry's replacement deletes its asset and the entry (or marks it deleted: true). Nothing new may import a listed module: `importers` records today's non-test consumers outside the ledger, a new one fails, and one that goes away must be pruned. Store delete_by follows the page that owns the same concept, defaulting to M3. /v1/confirms (#48) is omitted: no routes module for it exists in the tree. Enforced by scripts/check-workspace-retirement.py.",
